In `faker/proxy.py`, a missing provider attribute on a multi-locale proxy is handled by `__getattr__`, which calls `_select_factory(attr)` and then fetches that attribute from the returned factory. `_select_factory` always begins by calling `_map_provider_method(method_name)`. For a proxy built from a dict of locale weights, `__init__` stores `self._weights`, so when multiple factories support the method, `_select_factory` follows the `if weights:` branch and calls `_select_factory_distribution`; `_select_factory_choice` is only used when there are no weights. The test calls three distinct provider methods—`first_name()`, `last_name()`, and `name()`—so this `_select_factory` → `_map_provider_method` → `_select_factory_distribution` sequence occurs three times in that order.

